b. conducting counseling on improving women's quality of life;
c. conducting counseling on improving gender equality in family and community life;
d. conducting improvement of access and opportunities to receive information and economic resources through efforts to increase prosperous family income and increase women's economic productivity; ande. undertaking efforts to empower women heads of households.

Article 30

1. Law enforcement and legal assistance services are intended to provide assistance and protection to women victims of violence and witnesses with a gender-responsive approach so that victims obtain justice and legal certainty.
